From e5ad818d124132c72a89710a43c133f9f60c6b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iceyes <iceyes@iceyesdeMac-mini.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:02:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Make DingTalk login settings configurable via admin web
 UI

Move ENABLE_DINGTALK / DINGTALK_APP_KEY / DINGTALK_APP_SECRET from
static settings file to django-constance, so admins can edit them on
the sysadmin Settings page and changes take effect without restart.

- Add the three keys to CONSTANCE_CONFIG (file values become defaults)
- Convert module-level constants in seahub/dingtalk/settings.py to
  accessor functions; rewrite all import sites to dynamic reads
- Fix two module-level conditional imports that would break startup
- Register OauthRemoteUserBackend unconditionally (runtime gate by
  is_dingtalk_enabled() in views)
- Whitelist the keys in AdminWebSettings (allow empty secret/key)
- Add a DingTalk Login section to the sysadmin web-settings page
---
